step_7 recorded 0.879 A for a bare +1 with a designed charge set, 0.641 A inside
the oxygen van der Waals contact. The criterion here is 2.0-3.2 A, the range the
structural consensus gives for Arg-carboxylate salt bridges, because step_7's own
reframing is that inward motion is correct down to that distance and unphysical
only below it.

A FLAT tail means the approach has STOPPED, which is the result being tested, even
if the optimisation has not converged on every other coordinate.

NOTE ON THE PARAMETERS: the site carries sodium Lennard-Jones values taken from the
committed force field. A designed cation standing in for a guanidinium is not
sodium-sized, so a stopping distance at the short end of the range points at the
parameter, not at the mechanism. Burschowsky's 3.2 A is the calibration target.

